Cross toolchain for flash.tos
=============================

"make" here downloads the sources listed in Makefile (checked against
SHA256SUMS) and builds into install/:

  binutils 2.45, m68k-elf     patches/binutils-2.45-m68k-old-gas.patch: with
                              GAS_M68K_OLD set in the environment gas keeps 0(An),
                              assembles forward references as absolute long and
                              accepts a short branch to the next instruction,
                              like the gas of the original TOS builds
  gcc 3.3.2-mint              C files of the TOS part (boot, pmmu2.c, lz.c, ...);
                              32-bit host only, built in docker/ (needs docker)
  gcc 4.4.3-mint              drivers; patches/gcc-4.4.3-mint-pr39531.patch fixes
                              bclr/bset #31 on 64-bit hosts (PR target/39531)
  MiNTLib + fdlibm headers    patches/mintlib-2012-compat.patch makes them declare
                              what the 2012 MiNTLib did (no inline string functions,
                              strlen/strcmp without attributes, non-volatile _hz_200,
                              old XBIOS names, ...)

bin/ holds the commands the flash.tos Makefiles call:

  tos-gcc       TOS part: gcc 3.3.2 for C, gcc 4.4.3 preprocessor for .S, old gas mode
  drivers-gcc   drivers: gcc 4.4.3
  m68k-as       gas used like the MiNT a.out gas (.align, section padding, registers
                without %)

host/include/ maps the GEMDOS calls of the image tools (gentos, compress) to POSIX.

Build the images:

  make -C gnu
  make -C flash.tos firebee        (flash.tos/firebee/firetos.hex)
  make -C flash.tos ct60           (flash.tos/ct60/ctpcitos.bin, boot.hex, diag.hex)

GNU and GNU_PREFIX in the flash.tos Makefiles select another toolchain location.
